# ERP Lite

Canonical source for ERP-Lite-specific rules: `docs/features/ERP_Lite/RULES.md` — read it before writing ERP Lite code or migrations, and add any new ERP-Lite-only rule there (not here).

**Active now:** every NEW identifier owned by ERP Lite (DB objects, permission codes, feature flag keys, routes/folders, i18n namespaces, TS constant files) must carry the literal token `erplt`. DB pattern: `{scope}_erplt_{sub_feature}_{object_name}_{suffix}` (e.g. `org_erplt_fin_acct_mst`). Not retroactive — see `docs/features/ERP_Lite/RULES.md` §1 and the `/database` skill (`feature-abbreviations.md`, `conventions.md`) for the full rule and grandfathered exceptions.
